 Overview # After years using Wordpress for my personal blog, I decided to test something new. Wordpress works very well, but I think has become too heavy for a simple blog in the latest versions&hellip; Anyway&hellip; I found Ghost, a NodeJS blogging platform, that is actually in strong development but with all basic functionalities already.
Performance Comparison # The only thing I want to share for the moment is the performance test comparison. Sure, Wordpress didn&rsquo;t have exactly the same theme and could surely be better&hellip;
Wordpress: Ghost:

 Introduction # Every time I installed a new version of Fedora (I used to do a fresh installation to prevent any possible package errors/compatibility) I spent a lot of time reconfiguring my installation with the usual tweaks: installing additional repositories, configuring flash player (hoping it will die in the future), installing Java, &hellip;, &hellip;
What is Fedora Utils? # This time, while surfing the internet, I discovered Fedora Utils, an incredible project (simple but useful) that does all this configuration for you. You just need to select what you want and it will install everything for you. I know, it&rsquo;s not too difficult to create a simple bash script to do the same thing, but I&rsquo;m too lazy to spend time configuring my home desktop :)
Conclusion # Test it and enjoy.
